I can see the issue. The problem is with the Bootstrap grid structure. You have a row with g-0 (no gutters) that contains the sidebar and main content, but the main content has its own margin-left and width that conflicts with Bootstrap's column system.

Here's the fix - replace your existing CSS and add a critical fix to the HTML structure:

Fix 1: Update your CSS (replace the main-content section)

Replace your .main-content CSS with:

```css
/* Main Content - CRITICAL FIX */
.main-content {
    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
    padding: 30px;
    transition: var(--transition);
    min-height: 100vh;
    width: auto; /* Changed from calc(100% - var(--sidebar-width)) */
    flex: 1;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}

/* Fix for the container-fluid and row structure */
.container-fluid {
    padding: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
}

/* Ensure the row with sidebar and main content works properly */
.container-fluid > .row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: nowrap;
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
}

/* Sidebar needs to stay as is */
.sidebar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: var(--sidebar-width);
    position: relative; /* Changed from fixed */
    min-height: 100vh;
}

/* Main content should take remaining space */
.main-content {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0; /* Important for flex children */
    overflow-x: auto;
}
```

Fix 2: Update the HTML structure

Change the container-fluid div structure. Find this in your HTML:

```html
<div class="container-fluid p-0">
    <div class="row g-0">
        <!-- Sidebar -->
        <div class="sidebar">
```

And replace the entire container-fluid section with:

