Fix 3: Add this CSS to ensure proper flex behavior

Add this to your CSS:

```css
/* Critical flex fix */
body {
    overflow-x: hidden;
}

.d-flex {
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: flex-start;
    width: 100%;
}

/* Ensure sidebar doesn't break on mobile */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .container-fluid > .d-flex {
        flex-direction: column;
    }
    
    .sidebar {
        width: 100%;
        position: relative;
        min-height: auto;
    }
    
    .main-content {
        margin-left: 0 !important;
        width: 100% !important;
    }
}
```

Why this works:

The issue was that you were mixing Bootstrap's grid system (row and col classes) with custom CSS positioning. The sidebar was using position: fixed which takes it out of the document flow, while the main content was trying to calculate its width based on CSS variables.

The fix:

1. Changes the sidebar from position: fixed to position: relative (but keeps it visually in place using flexbox)
2. Uses flexbox instead of Bootstrap's grid for the main layout
3. Lets the main content naturally take the remaining space with flex: 1

This approach is more reliable and won't have the overlap issues you were experiencing.
